Usage: paste [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Merge lines of files.

Write lines consisting of the sequentially corresponding lines
from each FILE, separated by TABs, to standard output.
With no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.

Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.

Note: This implementation supports basic paste functionality.

OPTIONS:
  -d, --delimiters[=ARG]  reuse characters from LIST instead of TAB
  -s, --serial            paste one file at a time instead of in parallel
  -z, --zero-terminated   line delimiter is NUL, not newline
      --help              display this help and exit
  -V, --version           output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
